## 22. Definition of MVP done

The current MVP is ready only when all of the following are true for one exact commit:

- Every required capability in section 5.1 is implemented or explicitly removed through an approved PRD revision.
- All financial invariants, authorization boundaries, idempotency behavior, migrations, and generated contracts pass.
- The complete frontend and Go verification suites pass without ignored failures or weakened assertions.
- Every visual baseline change is manually approved.
- Real-stack financial, uncertainty, collaboration, dependency-failure, and recovery journeys pass against disposable data.
- No enabled action lacks its stated result or a visible unavailable reason.
- Responsive and accessibility gates pass for the supported device matrix.
- Exact-commit release evidence and known limitations are published.
- Named product and engineering owners approve local-MVP release.
- Any shared/pilot/production target additionally completes its applicable security, finance, legal, operations, infrastructure, recovery, device, and partner gates.

